%% openindex lock primitive — packages/cli/src/locks.ts
%% One impl, two API surfaces. Lifecycle + legend.

---
title: Lock lifecycle (single lock file at home/locks/name.lock)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> Free

    Free --> Acquired: acquire(name) — open wx [O_EXCL], write holder PID
    Free --> Stale: acquire(name) — EEXIST + isPidAlive(holder) false

    Stale --> Acquired: reclaim — unlink stale, retry open (bounded 3 attempts on EEXIST)
    Stale --> Free: another acquirer beat us to unlink

    Acquired --> Released: release(handle) — verify holder PID, then unlink
    Released --> Free: file gone
    Released --> [*]

    note right of Acquired
        O_EXCL guarantee:
        only one writer wins
        the create race. Body
        is holder PID as a
        decimal string.
    end note

    note right of Stale
        Liveness via signal 0
        (isPidAlive). ESRCH
        means dead, EPERM means
        alive. Bounded retry
        handles the race where
        two processes both see
        a stale lock.
    end note

